      "id": "https://www.paddlinglight.com/articles/1865-st-francis-canoe-build/",
      "url": "https://www.paddlinglight.com/articles/1865-st-francis-canoe-build/",
      "title": "[PaddlingLight.com] 1865 St. Francis Canoe Build",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.paddlinglight.com/pl/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/1000028690.webp\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.paddlinglight.com/pl/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/1000028690.webp\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.paddlinglight.com/pl/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/1000028690.webp\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.paddlinglight.com/pl/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/1000028690.webp\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<p>The 1865 St. Francis 2-Fathom Canoe appears as Figure 80 in The Bark Canoes and Skin Boats of North America, but until now I haven&#8217;t seen any replicas or semi-replicas built. Recently, Evan B. built a cedar strip canoe replica of the 1865 canoe. It turned out great and it&#8217;s fun to see these lines become a real canoe. Evan is sharing these, because he couldn&#8217;t find any photos online of this canoe. I couldn&#8217;t either back when I drafted the free canoe plans. You can see my drawing below. &#8220;The canoe handled great and was quite fast on the water,&#8221; Evan wrote. &#8220;The building process was a bit tricky when fiberglassing the inside of the bow and stern, but other than that, it wasn&#8217;t too bad. I wasn&#8217;t able to get any pictures of the canoe weighed down. It was solo my first trip.&#8221; The canoe looks great! Thanks for sharing the photos, Evan!</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.paddlinglight.com/articles/1865-st-francis-canoe-build/\">1865 St. Francis Canoe Build</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.paddlinglight.com\">PaddlingLight.com</a>. You can leave a comment by clicking here: <a href=\"https://www.paddlinglight.com/articles/1865-st-francis-canoe-build/\">1865 St. Francis Canoe Build</a>.</p>",
