      "title": "🔓 [Outside Online] I Fell 500 Feet Down the Maroon Bells Traverse and Lived. Here Is My Outlook on Risk.",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Hinkle1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Hinkle1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Hinkle1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Hinkle1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Hinkle1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<figure><img alt=\"I Fell 500 Feet Down the Maroon Bells Traverse and Lived. Here Is My Outlook on Risk.\" src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Hinkle1.jpg?width=1200\" /></figure>\n<p>Colorado hiker Brandon Hinkle was completing the Maroon Bells Traverse when he tumbled down a sheer rock face and suffered multiple serious injuries. Hinkle recounts his harrowing story of survival, and offers his perspective on risk taking in the outdoors. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com/outdoor-adventure/hiking-and-backpacking/maroon-bells-traverse-fall/\">I Fell 500 Feet Down the Maroon Bells Traverse and Lived. Here Is My Outlook on Risk.</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com\">Outside Online</a>.</p>",
